{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"14b8b90f-0c4b-47b6-b2bf-3803814525db","agentId":"abb8ac017b8de9178","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes, no searching. Memory limited: one 716px-wide CDP screenshot of the dossier at the end (cleanup via cuore/tests/_edge_cleanup.py). Report under 100 words. Files: cuore/web/templates/_feedback_panel.html, cuore/web/static/feedback.js, feedback.css, cuore/web/templates/base.html, _vbar.html, _vtabs.html, vehicle.html (blind spots and chips only), cuore/web/static/cuore.css (append marked section), cuore/web/static/cuore.js (the \"?\" keys overlay), cuore/tests/check_feedback_page.py, check_theme.py (adjust assertions you break). Do not edit bench.html, bench_bridge, checklists, dossier_bridge, _tools_panel (another agent). Spec: C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\research\\BENCH_UX_SPEC_2026-10-08.md items 12, 13, 14, 16, 17, 20. Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe.\n\nImplement: 12 The Ask/correct panel becomes a bottom sheet that PUSHES content (a fixed-height region reserved at the bottom while open, main gets padding-bottom equal to the sheet height) and is collapsed to the single FAB by default; never covers task text. 13 Per-element \"Flag this row\" affordance (reuse the data-fact mechanism) pre-filling the fact's context; reduce the verbs to three with one-line descriptions: Correct (this is wrong, here is the right value), Ask (a question about this), Confirm (I checked this on the car); map old kinds in feedback.js so the API still accepts them. 14 No hard truncation: blind-spot titles and header chips wrap, sentence case (no uppercase transform on those), vehicle name wraps to two lines before ellipsis; title attr keeps the full text. 16 One persistent tab bar: the bench page must get the same _vtabs.html strip; since bench.html is owned by another agent, make _vbar.html render the compact strip + _vtabs for tab == \"bench\" too (bench.html already includes _vbar? check `grep -n vbar cuore/web/templates/bench.html`; if it does not, report the one include line the other agent must add). 17 At 400-800 px only one floating element exists bottom-right (the FAB); the \"Stop Claude\" pill, if present in any template, moves in-flow under the status strip. 20 \"?\" keys overlay: make the `?` key open the existing #keyhelp panel (cuore.js) on every page, and the footer hint reads \"? keys\" only when it works. Checks (5): panel closed by default and main padding grows when opened (class toggles); three verbs present, five old radios absent; blind-spot heading not uppercase-truncated (full text present, no text-overflow ellipsis class); only one fixed bottom-right element at 716px (CDP bounding boxes); pressing \"?\" shows #keyhelp (CDP: dispatch key event, check hidden attr). Run check_feedback_page.py, check_theme.py, check_dossier_page.py."},"uuid":"55dd108a-d673-4881-935a-d4e1ba76d8b9","timestamp":"2026-10-08T17:36:41.301Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
