page's sticky strip)\n * wraps onto up to two lines before it falls back to an ellipsis, rather\n * than cutting off on line one. */\n.vline .vname {\n  white-space: normal; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis;\n  display: -webkit-box; -webkit-line-clamp: 2; line-clamp: 2;\n  -webkit-box-orient: vertical;\n}\n.vline { align-items: flex-start; }\n\n/* Item 17: at 400-800px the feedback FAB (base.html) is meant to be the\n * only floating bottom-right element on a page -- the dossier's own\n * quick-add-note FAB (vehicle.html) used to share that exact corner with\n * it. It keeps floating (it's still a useful one-tap shortcut), just from\n * bottom-left instead, so the two never compete for the same spot. */\n.fab-note { left: 18px; right: auto; }","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1412,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1412,"newLines":41,"lines":["   grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) !important;"," }"," .tw { max-width: 960px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }","+","+/* =========================================================================","+ * BENCH_UX_SPEC 2026-10-08, items 14 & 17.","+ * Appended section; everything above predates this pass. feedback.css","+ * carries items 12/13's own panel/kind-button rules -- this is just the","+ * bits that live in the shared sheet.","+ * ========================================================================= */","+","+/* Item 14: no hard truncation on a blind-spot title (vehicle.html) or the","+ * vbar's own header chips (_vbar.html's status-verdict/status-blocker/","+ * status-next, and the MES chip) -- `.chip-wrap` drops the chip's usual","+ * all-caps/no-wrap treatment for sentence case that wraps instead.","+ * title=\"\" (already present on every one of these) still carries the","+ * exact text for a tap/hover regardless. */","+.chip-wrap {","+  white-space: normal; text-transform: none; word-break: break-word;","+  max-width: none;","+}","+.vline .status-next.chip-wrap {","+  overflow: visible; text-overflow: clip; white-space: normal;","+}","+","+/* Item 14: the vehicle name (.vline .vname, every /v/ page's sticky strip)","+ * wraps onto up to two lines before it falls back to an ellipsis, rather","+ * than cutting off on line one. */","+.vline .vname {","+  white-space: normal; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis;","+  display: -webkit-box; -webkit-line-clamp: 2; line-clamp: 2;","+  -webkit-box-orient: vertical;","+}","+.vline { align-items: flex-start; }","+","+/* Item 17: at 400-800px the feedback FAB (base.html) is meant to be the","+ * only floating bottom-right element on a page -- the dossier's own","+ * quick-add-note FAB (vehicle.html) used to share that exact corner with","+ * it. It keeps floating (it's still a useful one-tap shortcut), just from","+ * bottom-left instead, so the two never compete for the same spot. */","+.fab-note { left: 18px; right: auto; }"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"930c7de7-f915-4a96-ab2b-a2ca122212e7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8b2ce6d7-901a-4fc1-b890-c16f9cfe1632","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
